# doorway-pair: a 4x4 siege unit and a 3x3 knight at the mouth of a channel one large body wide: the gap between two
# building wrecks of a destroyed base, cut from the audited 18-hour game at tick 432,000 (the cells are the
# wreck field there; the two movers are synthetic, with the footprints and the pace of the units that stood).
# One attack-move click for both. They meet at the mouth: the siege unit at origin (34,25) needs (35,25), whose cells
# the knight covers; the knight at (38,26) needs (37,26), whose cells the siege unit covers. Two footprints, so two planes
# and two groups, on fight legs: no swap, no funnel give-way, no yield. In the game the pair stood for good with
# its orders and an army queued behind it. Retail walks both through.
# Keys: g.S.arrived, g.K.arrived (1 each; 0 before the give-way in a knot), work.give_ways.total. Run at start
# offset 0: the gate offsets push the spawns into the wrecks.
scn 1
name doorway-pair
ticks 4500
seed 7
players 1
weapons off
map ascii
